    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math practical but not deeply passionate about it. As someone with upper secondary education, I use it for economics and daily problem-solving but don’t see it as a core interest. My parents’ educational backgrounds shaped my perspective—my mom’s lower secondary education made me appreciate applied math, while my dad’s PhD showed me its theoretical depth. I’m comfortable with basic calculations but prefer real-world applications over abstract proofs.",
